---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---
<Base
  title="Mission Vision Strategy | Organizational strategy, Chicago"
  description="Organizational strategy for mission-driven nonprofits, schools, research organizations, and media companies. Based in Chicago."
  current="home"
  contactHeading="Let's talk about what's next."
  contactText="Tell us a little about your organization and what you're working toward. We'll follow up to set up a conversation."
>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow"><img class="star" src="/images/star.svg" alt="">Chicago-based organizational strategy</p>
        <h1>Clear strategy for organizations built on a mission.</h1>
        <p class="lede">We help nonprofits, schools, research organizations, and media companies
          see where they stand, decide where they're going, and build the structures to get there.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="#contact">Start a conversation</a>
          <a class="button button-ghost" href="/services/">Explore services</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="skyline"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-warm">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow"><img class="star" src="/images/star.svg" alt="">Who we work with</p>
          <h2>Organizations where the work matters.</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="audiences">
          <li>Mission-driven nonprofits</li>
          <li>Schools &amp; educational institutions</li>
          <li>Research organizations</li>
          <li>Media companies</li>
          <li>Professional associations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow"><img class="star" src="/images/star.svg" alt="">Services</p>
          <h2>From assessment to a plan you can run.</h2>
          <p>Every engagement starts by listening to the people who do the work, and ends with
            something your team can actually use.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Organizational assessment</h3>
            <p>An honest read on governance, structure, operations, and capacity, with
              recommendations leadership can act on.</p>
            <a href="/services/#assessment">Learn more &rarr;</a>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Strategic planning</h3>
            <p>A shared direction and a roadmap to match, built with your board, staff, and
              stakeholders rather than handed to them.</p>
            <a href="/services/#planning">Learn more &rarr;</a>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Operations &amp; workflow design</h3>
            <p>Redesigned processes, clear roles, and practical tools, including AI-assisted
              workflows where they genuinely help.</p>
            <a href="/services/#operations">Learn more &rarr;</a>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Stakeholder research</h3>
            <p>Interviews, listening sessions, and analysis that turn what people say into
              programs and decisions.</p>
            <a href="/services/#research">Learn more &rarr;</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-warm" id="about">
      <div class="wrap split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow"><img class="star" src="/images/star.svg" alt="">About</p>
          <h2>Led by Kennen Hutchison.</h2>
          <p>Kennen is a former microbiologist turned organizational strategist. He has
            taught science, led student life at an independent school, and serves as the first
            Executive Director of the Association of Science Communicators.</p>
          <p>That range shapes the work: rigorous about evidence, fluent in how educators and
            nonprofits actually operate, and focused on plans people will use.</p>
          <ul class="work-list">
            <li><img class="star" src="/images/star.svg" alt=""><span>Designed an AI-assisted admissions review workflow for a Northwestern University certificate program, cutting review workload by 50%.</span></li>
            <li><img class="star" src="/images/star.svg" alt=""><span>Built a production framework for a 16-million-subscriber media organization that helped videos reach up to 200% of typical channel performance.</span></li>
            <li><img class="star" src="/images/star.svg" alt=""><span>Led organizational assessments for Chicago-area independent schools during periods of change.</span></li>
            <li><img class="star" src="/images/star.svg" alt=""><span>Grew a national professional association's membership 36% in eight months.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <p>&ldquo;Make no little plans.&rdquo;</p>
          <cite>Daniel Burnham, architect of the 1909 Plan of Chicago</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

</Base>
